/**
 * VirtualCircuitResource manages VirtualCircuits.
 *
 * There are two modes of VirtualCircuits: customer and provider.
 *
 * For customer, customers are allowed to set all settings.
 *
 * For provider, customers are allowed to set some subset of settings. Providers are allowed to set the rest.
 *
 * It is a security issue, if customers are allowed to set provider fields on a provider virtual circuit
 * and if providers are allowed to set customer fields on customer virtual circuits.
 *
 * VirtualCircuitResourceHelper handles validating which properties are allowed to be handled by home.
 * VirtualCircuitResource handles authentication and authorization.
 * VirtualCircuitBl handles validating that the settings are valid from a network / object standpoint.
 *
 * TODO: opc-request-id
 * TODO: Test e-tag stuff
 * TODO: Test if-match stuff
 */
